## Random-enchant jackpot is BiS

Rank a random-enchant green on the **best suffix it can roll** (top of that suffix’s range), not the expected value across every suffix.

- Superior Shoulders of Agility at 22 is **+6–7 Agi** (~9.5%). If that roll would be #1 in the slot, it **must** appear as BiS #1.
- `suffixChance` / the log hint tell the player the roll is slim. Chance never buries the hunt.
- Implemented in `pipeline/scripts/score.py` `best_variant` (`ROLL_POLICY="bestRoll"` ranks on jackpot).

## Leveling survivability (below 60)

Leveling is not raid min-max. Stamina, health, and armor beat a naked +1 primary-stat upgrade.

- Example: at 22, **Brawler’s / Trapper’s Leather Tunic** (8 Agi + stam / str / int) beat **Panther Armor** (9 Agi, no stam).
- `score.py` `weights_at_level()` multiplies sta / health / hp5 ×3 and armor ×2 when `level < 60`.

## Leveling endurance (below 60)

Survivability also means having and keeping mana. Call this **endurance**. It is less important than stamina, but it matters for most classes (paladin seals/heals, shaman shocks, hunter shots, caster drinks).

- `weights_at_level()` multiplies int / spirit / mp5 / mana ×2 when `level < 60` (stam is ×3).
- Level 60 uses the raw raid-scale weights. Forever level-60 guides may pin later; until then `GQ_NO_GUIDES=1`.

## Warrior tank is physical

Warrior Protection does not score spell power or healing. A glove with +SP / +healing (Silvered Gauntlets) ranks on the stamina, armor, and defense it actually has, in the same list as every other piece.

## Shaman Enhancement Tank is a hybrid

Like paladin Protection: 1h + shield, stamina/armor/defense first, then Rockbiter melee threat, then Earth Shock / Lightning Shield spell threat. Not dual-wield (Forever has no shaman DW). `enhancement_tank` in `weights.json`.

## Refreshed Forever tooltips (score from these)

Stored item facts must match the refreshed Wowhead Forever tooltip before a score. `refresh_forever_tips.py` writes those facts, then re-score. Do not score a row that still disagrees with the tooltip. Do not full-ingest to refresh tips (that replaces `sources.json` for id ≥ 200000). The 7 Oct 2026 pass updated 1186 items from nether tips and then re-scored all nine classes. Client pins stay: Coldflame, Silverlaine, Wolfsbane required level 20. Kaleidoscope resist 5 stays. Emit the audit **before** rescoring so recovered ids leave `FOREVER_MISSING`.

- The Equip line `Increases damage and healing done by magical spells and effects by up to N` is stored as **both** heal=N and damageDone=N. Do not strip it. Do not collapse it to spell power only. `forever_stats` folds damageDone into spell power so it is not counted twice. Holy uses the heal half. Mages (heal weight 0) use the damage half. An unequal "healing up to X and damage up to Y" stays heal=X, damageDone=Y (Staff of Westfall: 48 and 16). Skip party lines. A green `+N Spell Power` line is spell power only.
- **Required level is the tooltip `Requires Level`, never item level.** A stated level greater than 1 is never replaced. Fang of Magmatus is 13. Every item with **no** required level (or Wowhead's stub of 1) is assumed to be a quest reward, or some other gated source, until looked up. Find the quest on Wowhead Forever and set the required level to the **minimum** level that can pick up that quest (`Requires level N`; item XML `<json>` reqlevel, not `jsonEquip`, not the scaling minLevel). Several quests: take the lowest. A chain of at least five steps that must enter a dungeon uses that step's quest level when it is at least 8 levels above the pickup. Final Passage (Windstorm Hammer 6804, Dancing Flame 6806) is 36 because Test of Lore in Scarlet Monastery Library is level 36. Mage's Wand (7513, 7514, 11263) is 40 because Rituals of Power is level 40. Confront Yeh'kinya (20218, 20219) is 58. Drakefire Amulet (16309) is 60. Leaders of the Fang stays 10. The Defias Brotherhood stays 14. The item-level floor is only a stand-in until that lookup is done. Fang is not pinned over Golemheart.
- Cloaks, rings, necks, trinkets, and held items with `kind` `?` are `Misc`. `kind` `?` is not equippable.
- Weapon headers are labels only. If a staff is rank 1, main-hand rank 2 is the one-hand that off-hand rank 1 pairs with. A second staff may sit at rank 3 with a higher score than rank 2.
- Fishing and skinning are Profession. A crafted hunt states the Forever recipe skill on the line just before Source. A quest reward, including a seasonal quest, states `This quest can be picked up at level N.` on the line just before Source. N is the stored required level. The hunt list shows `#N` in faded grey in the collapse-icon column on every hunt row. N is that piece's place on the rank tooltip for the slot, including `#4` and later when an earlier piece was already obtained. A faction hole closes up, so the list number matches the tooltip. Each hunt row shows a small item icon immediately before the name, the same height as the row font. A question mark stands in until the client has the icon. Slot headers stay the plus and minus. The skill clause is green when the character meets the recipe and red when they are short or do not have the profession. The description does not repeat it: strip `Crafted with Leatherworking (requires skill N).` and list recipe materials there (`Materials: Light Leather (8), Coarse Thread (4).`) from the Wowhead Forever spell tooltip via `fetch_craft_skills.py --reagents`. Every new profession hunt, and every update of an existing profession hunt, looks that skill up in the same pass: ForeverDB `made` on `crafting/{id % 64}.json`, confirmed on the Wowhead Forever spell page (`Requires Leatherworking (40)`) when Wowhead is up. The item tooltip does not carry it. Run `fetch_craft_skills.py`. A skill of 1 is real when both say 1. Do not invent 1. Dress Shoes (6836) has no recipe. Container loot uses the Container filter. Boss drop has a dungeon flyout for the dungeons that have a boss-drop hunt at the current level, including lower ranks. Dungeon & Raid trash has the same flyout for trash hunts at the current level, and those boxes are separate from Boss drop. Hall of Thanes, Ruins of Lordaeron, and Excavation Site are on that list. Other is bosses that are not in a dungeon or raid. The flyouts do not scroll. Select all / Deselect all on the filter menu covers the source list and the profession, boss, and trash sub-filters. Play style sits at the bottom of the log. Five cards, names under the pictures, three then two. The green upgrade arrow is on both lists. It stays on the unfiltered best pieces when a filter or a play style hides them, and it stays on every hunt still showing, including a later rank, a notable, or a tracked hunt. Get it now can be on with either dungeon card, and with Don't look back and Buy it. No Dungeons and Dungeon Enjoyer turn each other off. Don't look back hides a hunt once its required level would be a gray quest (GetQuestGreenRange on the live character). Buy it keeps vendor pieces and anything that is not bind on pickup, unless a vendor sells that bind on pickup piece. No Dungeons hides hunts that send you into a dungeon or raid, including a quest that enters one at any step. A world drop stays even when its zone is a dungeon or raid name, or the pin is that entrance. Captain Melrache's Cape stays. World bosses and crafts you can buy stay. Dungeon Enjoyer keeps only those dungeon and raid hunts, so world bosses, crafts, vendors, and outdoor hunts stay hidden. Get it now hides a hunt until this character meets the standing stored on that item, or can make a bind-on-pickup craft. A bind-on-equip craft stays unless the item itself requires the profession to wear. Reaching the standing or the skill shows the hunt without turning the style off. An active filter hides source types that have no checkbox. The parchment shows `Rank #N` in a black box above the item title. N is that piece's place on the rank list this character can see. A hunt the other faction cannot get is left out and the numbers close up, for every class. A source filter or a play style does not change that number. Hovering the box says best, 2nd, 3rd, or 4th in that slot for a hunt on the unfiltered list. A hunt that only appears because a filter, a play style, or both are on gets the same line from tha