## Mage Battle Mage

Caster who swings. Specs: `battlemage_frost` (the hunt), `battlemage_fire`, `battlemage_arcane`. Spell power of that school first. Stamina base 0.15 (slightly above frost 0.1). Weapon `dpsWeight` 0.35. Coldflame Saber and Blade of Silverlaine stats are the Forever **client** tooltip, pinned in `client_item_overrides.json`. Do not sync the Wowhead nether tip back over them. The saber’s 98 Fire vs Frozen is every swing during a freeze (`FROZEN_MELEE_UPTIME` 25% frost, 15% fire/arcane). On an imbued weapon, printed stats stay the normal colors and only the imbue effect is grey. Do not repeat that effect. Add `Use: Combine the <base weapon> and <scroll>.` (`CLIENT_IMBUE` in `Data.lua`).

## GearQuest score (display only)

Hunt order stays `pipelineScore`. Do not call `GetItemInfo` while building the hover score, and cache `GetSlotRankList` plus `GearScoreContext` for the current level, spec, and equipped items. A scan must not call `GetItemInfo` for an item the client has not already cached. While item priming is suppressed, `IsItemDataCached` returns false instead of calling `GetItemInfo`, and `GetEquipSlot` and `GetItemArmorSubclass` return before `GetItemInfo` when the item is not cached. The score cache keeps every slot scored for this level, spec, and gear, so moving across a bag and back does not rebuild a slot. The score bar still must not call `GearScoreContext` once per slot. It uses `GearScoreWornRows` and `WornSlotIndex`. The obtain toast does not use this scan. It compares the looted item id to the hunt on the list. The tooltip index is display-only: best raw score in the slot at this level is **+100**, worst is **-100** (`GearScoreIndex`). Do not retune weights so the index matches the rank, and do not store the index on a pick. The line sits inside the item tooltip (hunt hover, character panel, chat, quest log) and on each (i) rank-list row. It is not on hunt-list rows. **General -> GearQuest score on tooltips** (`settings.showGearScore`, on when nil). Green `GQ-ArrowUp.png` / red `GQ-ArrowDown.png` compare to the equipped piece. Empty slot: index only. Rings and trinkets compare to the weaker piece only when both slots are filled. A worn piece that aged out of the band still compares (`EquippedPipelineScore`, nearest same-spec/faction band). Chat rank uses the active band, not `LEVEL_GRACE` (`EntryForItemLink`). **Kodohide Legguards** (285338) is rank 4 for Enhancement Horde at 25-27. **Pathfinder Belt** ranks only **of the Falcon**. If the piece is gear and not that ranked row, `GearScoreMissText` says why (suffix, level range, spec, class, faction, or no score). Bags, quivers, and ammo are skipped. Simulation shows **Turn off simulation mode to see your GearQuest Score for this item.** The Simulator button says **Turn off simulation**. A `setPiece` at `curatedRank` 1 whose stored score is below another piece in the slot adds **Rank 1 when you wear multiple pieces of this set.** Enhancement Horde 25-27: **Leggings of the Fang** (10410) rank 1 score 20.87; **Triprunner Dungarees** (9624) rank 2 score 21.56. Fang stays rank 1. Do not change `apply_embrace_package`. On the active hunt list, a slot header whose rank #1 the character already has (obtained, or worn) reads **- Rank #1 BiS acquired** after that header's (i). Among rank #1 pieces the character does not have, the three largest GearQuest score gains versus what is worn are marked **- Recommended** right after the item name, each with its own (i): "One of the best upgrades for your level. GearQuest marks up to three rank #1 pieces, the ones that improve what you are wearing the most." An empty slot is that piece's raw pipeline score, not an index jump from 0 to 100. It is recommended only when that score beats the raw gain of a rank #1 piece in a slot that already has gear. A downgrade is not recommended. A later rank is never the recommendation. Simulation hides both. Turning the score off hides the recommendation and leaves the acquired line. When you are not simulating, the log header is a four-section GearQuest score bar (average equipped index, slots below 0 count as 0, empty slots still show −100 and “(empty slot)”, clamped 0–100, 25 points a section, green then blue then purple then orange) with white “GearQuest Index Score - Collecting feedback on this” above it. Hover reads N / 100 · Below average (green), Fair (blue), Great (epic), or Legend (orange). Simulation keeps its header sentence. **General -> GearQuest score bar** (`settings.showGearScoreBar`, on when nil). Off hides the bar and shows the viewing-upgrades sentence. Equipping or removing gear refreshes the bar.

The **Play style** button reads **Play style*** while any play style is on.

Map pins are the addon's own frames on the canvas. Do not `AddDataProvider`, do not write `WorldMapFrame.pinPools`, do not hook `WorldMapFrame` OnShow, and do not `Hide()` a pin during the map's hide. That path taints `SetPreferredGamepadInteractTarget`. The world-drop icon is `GQ-WorldDrop.png`.

Dungeon upgrade sets are level **60** quests, not level 1. Classic Feralheart, Beastmaster, Heroism, The Five Thunders, Darkmantle, Deathmist, Soulforge, Virtuous, and Sorcerer's (72) plus the Forever spec copies (144) are those quests at gate 60, `questRaces` 0. Wrists: An Earnest Proposition. Hands and waist: Just Compensation. Feet, legs, shoulders: Anthion's Parting Words. Head and chest: Saving the Best for Last. The pin is the chain start, An Earnest Proposition. Those pieces stay locked at required level 60 in `DUNGEON_SET_60`. A quest lookup must not lower them to 58. Medal of Courage (6723) is 35. Zandalar Illusionist's Wraps (19846), Demoniac's Wraps (19848), Demoniac's Mantle (19849), Demoniac's Robe (20033), and Illusionist's Robe (20034) are 58. Leave out Beaststalker, Beastmaster's Girdle (5355), Darkmoon Card: Heroism, Uncle's Heroism, Violet Sorcerer's, Ogre Sorcerer Belt, and Sorcerer Collar. No quest and item level 15 or below, with no real Requires Level, is wearable at 1.

